    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on speed and prime lineup positioning to generate offensive production. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.27) and **Trea Turner** (67.76) stand as our elite plays, both benefiting from high-leverage leadoff spots and favorable matchup dynamics. **Trea Turner** is a particularly high-upside start against Freddy Peralta, as the opponent\u2019s slow delivery significantly bolsters the probability of a multi-SB performance, a critical advantage given our scarcity-focused strategy. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (66.32) remains a plug-and-play cornerstone despite the sub-optimal platoon matchup against Joey Cantillo, as his elite 0.450 xwOBA provides the necessary floor to justify a start in any environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer was the exclusion of **Colt Keith**, whose score of 53.46 narrowly missed the cut behind the projected efficiency of **Jacob Gonzalez** (56.24). While **Colt Keith** benefits from favorable wind conditions, he is handicapped by an assumed 8th-spot batting order, whereas **Jacob Gonzalez** leverages a stronger platoon advantage against Troy Melton. We are monitoring the lineups closely for **Christian Yelich** and **Dillon Dingler**; **Christian Yelich** is currently carrying a high-risk profile (42.50) due to a brutal matchup against Chris Sale, and any late-breaking news regarding his status or weather concerns in that stadium could see him swapped for a more stable bench option. \n\nManagers should also remain cautious with **Casey Schmitt** (44.51), whose score is tethered to a tight matchup against Max Meyer. While his platoon split is favorable, the presence of an elite hold pitcher on the mound limits his ceiling for stolen bases today. We are playing for consistent accumulation across all five categories, but prioritize keeping **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** active to insulate us against the volatility of the lower-tier starters like **Christian Yelich** and **Casey Schmitt**.",
